y aspect of  the business it's all i ever wanted to  do part of the business at luigi's an  appreciation of golf which started with  her grandfather chuck he loved the  masters tournament and back in the early  days of the tournament when it wasn't  you know it was anybody could buy a  badge  he would buy tickets and hand them out  to help promote and just customers yes  and he was there used to be a master's  parade and he was the chairman for the  parade masters week the busiest of the  year for luigi's back when penelope's  grandfather ran things and now people  used to walk up and ask my grandfather  how long is the weight and he would say  don't ask just get we serve cocktails  while people wait to just get a drink  and enjoy the company out here  and you get a seat when you get a seat  her grandfather was also the one who  started this collection of masters  badges which her father has proudly  added to these date back to 63. wow do  you know how much this is worth i don't  i don't we get you know people come in  and want to make offers on it every year  while penelope says it's not for sale  there's one thing her family treasures  even more when it comes to the masters  every year you see the same faces come  through sometimes some new faces but the  same customers come in from all  different parts of the world  and it's not just the masters patrons  ben crenshaw comes and sees us every  year he's one of our favorites we have a  soft spot for a gentleman you lit up  right there  because he's such a genuine person  and his wife julie and their girls let  me see they all come in  the nicholas family would eat with us  every year um the pilots would come eat  with us and take food back to the air  bear  so i mean it's just lots of traditions  just like passing on the family business  i would come and work you know side by  side with my dad just during the  transition  as he did with his father and his father  did with his father and you were telling  me about your daughter she just has the  knack it's just in her blood and we have  such a big family i can't imagine that  there won't be that love among  someone in the fifth generation so our  goal is definitely to keep it moving  forward luigi's going on  many generations that's our that's our  plan hit the century mark that's it  and we could not ship luigi's back to  you guys but i wanted you to be able to  eat and i wanted to keep with tradition  so like i have the pimento cheese and  egg salad sandwiches here i know you  have them back in studio  i've been enjoying them every day along  with a crow's nest so i hope you guys  enjoy just a little taste of the masters  that i was able to send you  you know when i lived in columbia south  carolina pimento cheese was my go-to  sandwich because you know i didn't eat  meat  this was it and you got to put potato  chips in it and how much of these cost  there dollar fifty dollar wow that's it  so good isn't that great classic good  stuff

